Wed Nov 11 19:46:51 UTC 2026 - Harshvardhan Sharma <harshvardhan.sharma@suse.com>

- Update to version 1.6.0: upgrade all roles; fix the ssh role on
  SLE 16.1 and semanage-based selinux settings on SLE 16
- The 18 roles from linux-system-roles are built from their
  <version>-suse tags: the named upstream release plus the upstream
  changes up to 2026-11-11. ha_cluster, mssql and auto_maintenance
  are the unmodified upstream releases
- Roles check their variables against an argument spec; a value of
  the wrong type stops the role before it changes anything (not yet
  in ha_cluster and mssql)
- postgresql on SUSE installs postgresqlNN-server and honours
  postgresql_version (16, 17 or 18, default 18). On a host with
  another major version installed the role stops with a message and
  changes nothing until postgresql_version is set to that version;
  a server set up by the previous role version on SLE 15 SP7 is
  version 17
- aide, certificate, journald, keylime_server, logging, network,
  postfix and postgresql handle transactional hosts like the other
  roles: with packages staged they reboot if
  <role>_transactional_update_reboot_ok is true and fail if it is
  unset
- Roles write a begin and a success record of each run to syslog
  (new in 16 roles; not in himmelblau, mssql and suseconnect)
- Update role versions:
  - firewall 1.11.6 -> 1.14.0:
    - add firewalld policies
    - keep the ipset family when an ipset is removed and follow
      FlushAllOnReload for runtime ipsets
    - rich rule handling and firewall_config reset are idempotent
    - install python311-firewall on openSUSE Leap 15
  - timesync 1.11.4 -> 1.15.0:
    - support SLES 16 and openSUSE Leap 16
    - support key and keyfile for NTP authentication
    - add timesync_restart_immediate
  - journald 1.5.2 -> 1.8.0
  - ssh 1.7.1 -> 1.9.1:
    - fix the role on SLE 16.1: create /etc/ssh/ssh_config.d when
      it is missing
    - on SUSE, a written /etc/ssh/ssh_config keeps the vendor
      includes and defaults
    - use the primary group of ssh_user for ~/.ssh
  - crypto_policies 1.5.2 -> 1.9.0:
    - add crypto_policies_force_regenerate
  - systemd 1.3.7 -> 1.5.2:
    - add file_content for unit files and drop-ins
    - fix unit state reporting with ansible-core 2.19 and later
  - postfix 1.6.6 -> 1.10.0:
    - add postfix_secure_logging and postfix_additional_packages
  - postgresql 1.5.1 -> 1.9.0:
    - add postgresql_secure_logging
  - certificate 1.5.0 -> 1.10.0:
    - manage system certificate trust, CA certificates and
      blocklist entries
    - pass an issuer to the provider
  - selinux 1.11.1 -> 1.13.1:
    - install semanage on SLES 16 and openSUSE Leap 16; booleans,
      ports, logins, file contexts and the purge options failed
      without it
    - load policy modules before they are referenced
    - add ignore_module_cache
    - report module changes in check mode
  - podman 1.9.2 -> 1.14.3:
    - add podman_run_as_ansible_user
    - restart services when their dependencies change
    - prune unused images before pulling new ones
    - support kube specs with several Kubernetes objects
    - create host directories for quadlet Volume entries
  - cockpit 1.7.4 -> 1.10.0:
    - install cockpit-bootloader on SLE 16.1; SLES for SAP 16 and
      openSUSE Leap 16 use the SLES 16 package set
  - aide 1.2.5 -> 1.5.0:
    - better check mode support
  - keylime_server 1.2.4 -> 1.4.1
  - kernel_settings 1.3.8 -> 1.6.0
  - network 1.18.0 -> 1.21.1:
    - no package install on every run on SLE 16
    - retry reading an unstable device
    - describe NetworkManager changes in check mode
  - sudo 1.2.9 -> 1.5.0:
    - support continuation lines in scan_sudoers
  - logging 1.16.0 -> 1.17.1
  - ha_cluster 1.31.3 -> 1.32.2:
    - the upstream release; no change to the crmsh code SUSE uses
  - suseconnect 1.0.2 -> 1.0.3:
    - mask the registration code in the registration failure
      message
    - support SLES 16.1 Immutable
    - require ansible-core 2.18 or later
  - auto_maintenance 1.120.5 -> 2.5.0 (build tool, not in the
    package)
  - himmelblau 1.2.0 -> 2.1.0 (SLE 16.1 only):
    - require ansible-core 2.20 or later
    - check login scoping on every run, also with
      configure_pam: false, and refuse an unsafe PAM stack
    - transactional hosts: no reboot on a re-run while packages
      are staged but not yet live
    - write a list in himmelblau_extra_config comma-separated

